            <ArticleTitle>Denervation hyperpathia: a convulsive syndrome of the spinal cord responsive to carbamazepine therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>287-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two cases of denervation hyperpathia that responded well to treatment with carbamazepine are presented. A theoretical relation of this disorder to trigeminal neuralgia and focal seizures is emphasized in the light of experimental data and clinical characteristics.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
